# File: tests/features/add_greeting_blake2s_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/284-add-greeting-blake2s-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Return the BLAKE2s hex digest of the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Return the BLAKE2s hex digest of the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_blake2s is called with Ada and Ada Lovelace
    Then the results are the 64-character hex strings 68d52139de7dbb117ec790dad9989297d2dc4914ebd9b4d177d0e5da344edb14 and 22f894a44c4420a35fdf533cbb7b73908b46f9e0733f84cc89e964994a9631e7

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Hash the UTF-8 encoding of non-ASCII greetings
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_blake2s is called with Zo plus U+00EB
    Then the result is 8092041e5f4bb16247b07aa2d091daf95dae26f1a9ad10f3def9ebfe616b4b3b, the hashlib BLAKE2s hex digest of the UTF-8 encoded greeting

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_blake2s is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_blake2s of Ada
    Then it prints the Ada BLAKE2s digest and greeting_blake2s is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the lowercase hex UTF-8 default-parameter BLAKE2s result, completed-greeting scope, and inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0
